        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Silent World, Zeitgeist film series\n- People: Jacques-Yves Cousteau, Louis Malle, Peter Joseph\n- Events: 1956 Cannes Film Festival\n- Concepts: Documentary films, conspiracy theories, social and economic change\n\nFacts:\n- The Silent World is a 1956 French documentary film co-directed by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- At the 1956 Cannes Film Festival, the Palme d'Or went to The Silent World by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- Zeitgeist is a series of three documentary films released between 2007 and 2011.\n- The Zeitgeist film series presents conspiracy theories and proposals for broad social and economic changes.\n- Peter Joseph is best known for the Zeitgeist film series.\n- Peter Joseph wrote, directed, narrated, scored, and produced the Zeitgeist film series.",
